<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia says oil prices above budget forecast.</title>
<headline>Indonesia says oil prices above budget forecast.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesian Finance Minister Mar'ie Muhammad said on Tuesday oil prices in the first half of fiscal 1996/97 (April-March) rose to an average of $19.15 a barrel and would continue at that level for the rest of the year.</p>
<p>In its budget for the fiscal year, Indonesia had forecast a price of $16.50 a barrel.</p>
</text>
